{"name":"Red Velvet","hex":"#783b38","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red velvet","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Cocoa flavor with red coloring.","A red-velvet-flavored food item."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red_velvet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Red velvet cake","blocks":[{"text":"Red velvet cake is a red-colored layer cake with cream cheese or ermine icing. The origin of the cake is unknown, although it is popular in the Southern United States and has been served as a dessert at New York City's Waldorf-Astoria hotel since the 1920s. Both the hotel and Eaton's in Canada claim to have developed the recipe. Ingredients of the cake include baking powder, butter, buttermilk or vinegar, cocoa powder, eggs, flour, salt, vanilla extract, and, in most modern recipes, red food coloring. The cake's popularity declined after Red Dye #2 was linked to cancer in the 1970s but has since improved in the United States and elsewhere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Red_Velvet_Cake_Waldorf_Astoria.jpg/330px-Red_Velvet_Cake_Waldorf_Astoria.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_velvet_cake","wikidata":"Q1284887"},{"title":"Red Velvet (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Red Velvet is a 2008 American independent horror film directed by Bruce Dickson and written by Anthony Burns and Joe Moe. The film stars Henry Thomas and Kelli Garner and is the final film of Forrest J Ackerman."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9e/Red_Velvet_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Velvet_(film)","wikidata":"Q7305189"},{"title":"Red Velvet (group)","blocks":[{"text":"Red Velvet (Korean: 레드벨벳) is a South Korean girl group formed and managed by SM Entertainment. They originally debuted on August 1, 2014, with the single \"Happiness\" with the four-member line-up of Irene, Seulgi, Wendy, and Joy. A fifth member, Yeri, joined in March 2015, with the release of their first extended play, the chart-topping Ice Cream Cake. Sonically, the music of Red Velvet reflects their group name: their predominantly-pop \"red\" side experiments occasionally with electronic and funk, while their \"velvet\" side focuses on '90s-influenced R&B with elements of ballad and hip hop."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/%EB%A0%88%EB%93%9C%EB%B2%A8%EB%B2%B3%28Red_Velvet%29_%EC%BC%80%EC%9D%B4%EC%BD%98_%EC%9E%AC%ED%8C%AC_2024_%EB%A0%88%EB%93%9C%EC%B9%B4%ED%8E%AB_KCON_JAPAN_2024_%281%29.jpg/330px-%EB%A0%88%EB%93%9C%EB%B2%A8%EB%B2%B3%28Red_Velvet%29_%EC%BC%80%EC%9D%B4%EC%BD%98_%EC%9E%AC%ED%8C%AC_2024_%EB%A0%88%EB%93%9C%EC%B9%B4%ED%8E%AB_KCON_JAPAN_2024_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Velvet_(group)","wikidata":"Q17466114"},{"title":"Velvet","blocks":[{"text":"Velvet is a type of woven fabric with a dense, even pile that gives it a distinctive soft feel. Historically, velvet was typically made from silk. Modern velvet can be made from silk, linen, cotton, wool, synthetic fibers, silk-cotton blends, or synthetic-natural fiber blends."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Blue_velvet_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Blue_velvet_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Velvet","wikidata":"Q243519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Red_devil%27s_food.png/500px-Red_devil%27s_food.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Red_devil%27s_food.png/1280px-Red_devil%27s_food.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Red_devil%27s_food.png/500px-Red_devil%27s_food.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A recipe for \"Red Devil's Food\" from the 1927 edition of Ladies' Home Journal","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARed_devil's_food.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Original_Red_Velvet_Recipe_Card.jpg/500px-Original_Red_Velvet_Recipe_Card.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Original_Red_Velvet_Recipe_Card.jpg/500px-Original_Red_Velvet_Recipe_Card.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The red velvet cake recipe by Adams Extract","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOriginal_Red_Velvet_Recipe_Card.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/KCON_2015_Red_Velvet.jpg/500px-KCON_2015_Red_Velvet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/KCON_2015_Red_Velvet.jpg/1280px-KCON_2015_Red_Velvet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/KCON_2015_Red_Velvet.jpg/500px-KCON_2015_Red_Velvet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Red Velvet at KCON 2015 in Los Angeles","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKCON_2015_Red_Velvet.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Red_Velvet_at_Incheon_Hallyu_K-pop_Concert_in_October_2015_01.jpg/500px-Red_Velvet_at_Incheon_Hallyu_K-pop_Concert_in_October_2015_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Red_Velvet_at_Incheon_Hallyu_K-pop_Concert_in_October_2015_01.jpg/1280px-Red_Velv